    {
      "id": 97783,
      "name": "Braithwhite",
      "username": "Braithwhite",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/braithwhite/{size}/1854_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-03-28T20:27:28.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I have a gut feeling that the operative is going to go with an all-female crew.</p><p>From left to right, my best guesses are:</p><p>Far left: Ermine: We know she's adept at being a distraction, and is a highly skilled thief. &nbsp;We also know that she desperately wants to get back into the good life. &nbsp;Being a part of the Operative's new organization would give her back the veneer of respectability, and allow her to continue her rooftop running.</p><p>Mid left: someone with a truly amazonian phsyique. &nbsp;She is also standing at the operative's right hand, so &nbsp;my guess is that this woman is the Operative's muscle for when she can't be in two places at once.</p><p>Center: No idea.</p><p>Mid right: I'm thinking that this might be the mirror woman who battles setback. &nbsp;</p><p>Far right: I'm thinking that this might be Highbrow. &nbsp;We see her in a sort of command chair in Vengeance, and given how the operative was filled full of arrows on her incap, having somoen who is a nemesis of Parse might not be a bad idea...</p><p><span>Alt far right: another intriguing possibility is this is Miss Information. &nbsp;She's at her most danagerous behind the scenes, and functioning as the Operative's information coordinator could serve her own interests. &nbsp;One of parse's cards has Miss information in front of a broken cyclohexane vat, being covered in toxic goo- perhaps she now requires a life-support chair?</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 6,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:25:14.955Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
