      "raw": "<p>I have a gut feeling that the operative is going to go with an all-female crew.</p><p>From left to right, my best guesses are:</p><p>Far left: Ermine: We know she&#39;s adept at being a distraction, and is a highly skilled thief. &nbsp;We also know that she desperately wants to get back into the good life. &nbsp;Being a part of the Operative&#39;s new organization would give her back the veneer of respectability, and allow her to continue her rooftop running.</p><p>Mid left: someone with a truly amazonian phsyique. &nbsp;She is also standing at the operative&#39;s right hand, so &nbsp;my guess is that this woman is the Operative&#39;s muscle for when she can&#39;t be in two places at once.</p><p>Center: No idea.</p><p>Mid right: I&#39;m thinking that this might be the mirror woman who battles setback. &nbsp;</p><p>Far right: I&#39;m thinking that this might be Highbrow. &nbsp;We see her in a sort of command chair in Vengeance, and given how the operative was filled full of arrows on her incap, having somoen who is a nemesis of Parse might not be a bad idea...</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">Alt far right: another intriguing possibility is this is Miss Information. &nbsp;She&#39;s at her most danagerous behind the scenes, and functioning as the Operative&#39;s information coordinator could serve her own interests. &nbsp;One of parse&#39;s cards has Miss information in front of a broken cyclohexane vat, being covered in toxic goo- perhaps she now requires a life-support chair?</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
